import lib/process.dl
import lib/text.dl

function the test interpreter for termination handlers:
    execute:
        return "python" if the process platform is Windows, else "python3"

class:
    patterns:
        [a|] reading state
    members:
        success as a boolean
        completion as a boolean
        stream ending as a boolean

function {reading state:state} succeeded:
    replacement:
        state's success

function {reading state:state} is complete:
    replacement:
        state's completion

function {reading state:state} is incomplete:
    replacement:
        the inverse of state's completion

function {reading state:state} awaits the stream ending:
    replacement:
        the inverse of state's stream ending

function {reading state:state} should continue:
    replacement:
        (state succeeded) and ((state is incomplete) and (state awaits the stream ending))

set command to a process command for the test interpreter for termination handlers
add "-u" as an argument to command
add "-c" as an argument to command
add "import os,signal,sys,time\nif os.name != 'nt': signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, lambda *_: sys.exit(0))\nprint('ready')\ntime.sleep(30)" as an argument to command
launch command and set child to it

set contents to the string form of ""
set reading to @intrinsic("construct", a reading state, true, false, false)
loop while reading should continue:
    read the standard output of child and set chunk to it
    set reading's success to chunk succeeded
    if reading succeeded:
        set contents to (contents + chunk's contents)
        set reading's completion to contents ends with "\n"
        set reading's stream ending to chunk reached the end of stream
terminate child and set termination to it
wait for child and set status to it
set expected to 0 as a 64 bit integer
if the process platform is Windows:
    set expected to 1 as a 64 bit integer

print whether child was launched as a line
print whether (reading succeeded) and (reading is complete) as a line
print whether (contents = "ready\n") as a line
print whether termination succeeded as a line
print whether status succeeded as a line
print whether status reports completion as a line
print whether status reports termination as a line
print whether (status's exit code = expected) as a line
print whether (status's termination signal = (0 as a 32 bit integer)) as a line
